477
00:30:56,901 --> 00:30:58,940
which helps them do their jobs much more effectively.

478
00:31:00,580 --> 00:31:03,120
And we can clearly see he has a weapon on the ground,

479
00:31:03,480 --> 00:31:07,400
he has a shovel in his hand, and he appears to be digging a hole.

480
00:31:08,360 --> 00:31:10,300
We've gotten really good feedback from the field

481
00:31:10,301 --> 00:31:13,740
where soldiers have been able to get intelligence just like this.

482
00:31:16,720 --> 00:31:19,560
When troops need a smaller, even more mobile UAV,

483
00:31:20,080 --> 00:31:21,360
they can turn to the Raven.

484
00:31:22,580 --> 00:31:26,120
Raven is the most prolific unmanned aircraft in the world today.

485
00:31:26,121 --> 00:31:30,860
We've shipped more than 15,000 of these little airplanes to customers all over the world.

486
00:31:31,520 --> 00:31:36,700
The Raven is more concealable than the Puma, but it can only stay airborne for 90 minutes.

487
00:31:39,200 --> 00:31:45,260
Aeroviron's smallest UAV, the Wasp, is roughly the size of a hobbyist's remote-controlled plane.

488
00:31:45,960 --> 00:31:48,680
Less is definitely more for our military customers.

489
00:31:49,340 --> 00:31:53,700
The Wasp is the smallest unmanned aircraft system in the world today.

490
00:31:53,701 --> 00:31:57,500
It weighs about a pound. It flies for about 45 minutes.

491
00:31:57,501 --> 00:32:00,100
It can be packed inside of a backpack.

492
00:32:00,101 --> 00:32:02,500
You just throw it in the air and it flies away.

493
00:32:02,501 --> 00:32:06,140
The WASP's small size and quiet electric motor

494
00:32:06,141 --> 00:32:08,340
make it nearly undetectable from the ground.

495
00:32:08,341 --> 00:32:12,820
Tiny, stealthy, unmanned aircraft are the perfect tools

496
00:32:12,821 --> 00:32:14,460
for troops facing sniper fire.

497
00:32:14,461 --> 00:32:17,460
Once they know where the enemy is hiding,

498
00:32:17,461 --> 00:32:19,100
they can lower the hammer.

499
00:32:19,101 --> 00:32:21,460
Get down! Put the weapon down!

500
00:32:21,461 --> 00:32:22,700
Land in the stomach!

501
00:32:22,701 --> 00:32:26,440
Sergeant.

502
00:32:26,441 --> 00:32:28,240
These are used by front-line war fighters.

503
00:32:28,241 --> 00:32:29,440
They have to be small.

504
00:32:29,441 --> 00:32:31,660
They have to be light.

505
00:32:31,661 --> 00:32:34,060
These mini UAVs also have to be tough.

506
00:32:34,061 --> 00:32:39,020
There have been cases where insurgents have actually hit these aircraft, put a hole in

507
00:32:39,021 --> 00:32:43,040
a wing, and when they bring it back, they can just take a roll of duct tape and put

508
00:32:43,041 --> 00:32:46,140
it on, tape it up, and send it right back out in the air.

509
00:32:46,141 --> 00:32:48,940
The biggest beating can come on landing.

510
00:32:48,941 --> 00:32:52,580
So the UAVs are built to break apart upon impact.

511
00:32:52,581 --> 00:32:57,720
Kevlar is a material that we use to ensure the strength and the lightness of these aircraft.

512
00:32:58,560 --> 00:33:01,040
When you see the kind of beating these take out in the field,

513
00:33:01,300 --> 00:33:04,260
you'll understand why we need to make sure this is very, very durable.

514
00:33:04,880 --> 00:33:06,400
But the pieces don't break.

515
00:33:06,620 --> 00:33:08,600
The troops can actually snap them back together.

516
00:33:11,380 --> 00:33:15,500
Aerovironment has one more UAV in development that can deliver a blow of its own.

517
00:33:16,040 --> 00:33:19,100
We've also been developing a totally new kind of a system,

518
00:33:19,101 --> 00:33:23,040
which is actually more like a munition than an unmanned aircraft system.

519
00:33:23,120 --> 00:33:24,340
We call that the switchblade.

520
00:33:25,140 --> 00:33:28,520
The tiny switchblade is fired from a launch tube on the ground.

521
00:33:29,420 --> 00:33:33,060
As the plane approaches its target, the onboard explosive is armed.

522
00:33:33,820 --> 00:33:36,020
The switchblade then flies into that target

523
00:33:36,021 --> 00:33:39,140
and detonates taking out that target and removing the threat.

524
00:33:42,640 --> 00:33:45,660
While the switchblade will deliver a small, precise payload,

525
00:33:45,661 --> 00:33:52,720
The goal of a nuclear bomb is to unleash as much destruction as possible.

526
00:33:53,720 --> 00:34:00,140
During the Cold War, the United States and the Soviet Union raced to build ever bigger bombs and missiles.

527
00:34:01,160 --> 00:34:03,500
Weapons capable of wiping out entire cities.

528
00:34:07,760 --> 00:34:09,560
But we also thought small.

529
00:34:09,561 --> 00:34:16,740
In the 1950s and 60s, a Soviet invasion of what was then West Germany seemed very possible.

530
00:34:17,400 --> 00:34:20,720
The United States wanted a weapon that could stop the Soviets' cold.

531
00:34:21,780 --> 00:34:24,340
So they created miniature nuclear bombs.

532
00:34:27,440 --> 00:34:33,840
The United States military in the 1950s actually developed an atomic recoilless rifle,

533
00:34:34,240 --> 00:34:35,740
kind of like an atomic bazooka.

534
00:34:36,120 --> 00:34:38,040
It was nicknamed the Davy Crockett.

535
00:34:38,041 --> 00:34:42,820
When you start to miniaturize atomic weapons, they become tactical.

536
00:34:42,980 --> 00:34:46,200
They can actually be used for the first time on the battlefield,

537
00:34:46,400 --> 00:34:48,280
and that completely changes the equation.

538
00:34:48,900 --> 00:34:54,280
The Davy Crockett carried the lightest nuclear warhead on record, the W-54.

539
00:34:55,640 --> 00:34:59,000
At 11 inches in diameter and weighing 51 pounds,

540
00:34:59,880 --> 00:35:04,300
the W-54 was small and light enough to be carried by one man.

541
00:35:04,301 --> 00:35:10,660
had a tripod. You could download it or actually fire it from the Jeep itself.

542
00:35:11,340 --> 00:35:14,110
The Davy Crockett's range was about two miles.

543
00:35:14,111 --> 00:35:16,760
And so depending on the power of the warhead

544
00:35:16,761 --> 00:35:20,300
and the direction of the wind, the operating team could be in danger.

545
00:35:25,080 --> 00:35:29,760
With the more powerful explosive heads that were used on the Davy Crockett, there's actually a

546
00:35:29,761 --> 00:35:34,620
that the range of the kill zone is greater than the effective range of the weapon,

547
00:35:34,760 --> 00:35:36,380
making it a weapon of last resort.

548
00:35:37,080 --> 00:35:40,820
The Davy Crockett was tested several times, but never used in combat.

549
00:35:42,460 --> 00:35:46,820
Eventually, the weapon was stockpiled and then decommissioned in 1971.

550
00:35:49,300 --> 00:35:52,880
We've seen how advances in technology have made weapons smaller,

551
00:35:53,240 --> 00:35:55,200
more maneuverable,

552
00:35:55,680 --> 00:35:57,860
but just as deadly.

553
00:35:59,760 --> 00:36:02,760
These tiny tools make fighting more efficient,

554
00:36:03,240 --> 00:36:05,640
both for the good guys and the bad.

555
00:36:08,300 --> 00:36:11,240
But another, more secret group of weapon wielders

556
00:36:11,241 --> 00:36:13,980
relies on miniature devices to survive.

557
00:36:14,920 --> 00:36:15,620
Spies.

558
00:36:15,800 --> 00:36:17,720
When you start to get into the realm of spies,

559
00:36:17,880 --> 00:36:20,940
you're talking about miniaturized and unusual weapons,

560
00:36:21,020 --> 00:36:22,880
really of types that almost boggle the mind.

561
00:36:23,480 --> 00:36:24,400
Cigarette packs.

562
00:36:25,480 --> 00:36:26,220
Lipstick cases.

563
00:36:27,220 --> 00:36:30,200
Even pens have all been transformed into firearms.

564
00:36:31,480 --> 00:36:35,480
The intelligence community is incredibly creative when it comes to tiny weapons.

565
00:36:36,360 --> 00:36:40,940
One of the more interesting cases was actually an umbrella used to deliver a poison dart.

566
00:36:41,980 --> 00:36:49,000
In 1978, Bulgarian dissident Georgi Markov was killed when a tiny pellet of ricin was injected into his leg.

567
00:36:49,800 --> 00:36:52,180
They figured out what happened during the autopsy.

568
00:36:52,680 --> 00:36:54,640
Almost anything can be disguised.

569
00:36:54,641 --> 00:36:56,400
is really quite amazing.

570
00:36:57,340 --> 00:36:59,420
Spies may have an arsenal of secret weapons,

571
00:36:59,720 --> 00:37:01,480
but they're not alone.

572
00:37:03,340 --> 00:37:04,920
Irv Miller and his wife Laura

573
00:37:04,921 --> 00:37:07,120
have been developing tiny self-defense weapons

574
00:37:07,121 --> 00:37:09,660
for civilians, police, and corrections officers.

575
00:37:10,680 --> 00:37:13,300
At some point in everybody's life, they get scared.

576
00:37:13,740 --> 00:37:16,880
Having some type of self-defense weapon on you is a good idea.

577
00:37:17,840 --> 00:37:20,540
Irv bought his first stun gun more than 20 years ago

578
00:37:20,541 --> 00:37:23,560
and got instantly hooked on small, less lethal weapons.

579
00:37:24,640 --> 00:37:27,560
Not every situation calls for a lethal action.

580
00:37:28,400 --> 00:37:30,420
Lethal actions are literally life and death.

581
00:37:31,960 --> 00:37:34,820
One of IRB's bestsellers is the couboutin.

582
00:37:35,360 --> 00:37:40,280
This slim impact weapon packs a punch in less than six inches of aluminum or plastic.

583
00:37:40,281 --> 00:37:43,840
What makes it so effective is that there's pressure points all over the body.

584
00:37:44,960 --> 00:37:49,160
Understanding the body's various pressure points is key to mastering the couboutin.

585
00:37:49,660 --> 00:37:54,040
If you take a hard object like a couboutin, you press that anywhere around the wrist

586
00:37:54,041 --> 00:37:56,040
and squeeze from the other side with your thumbs,

587
00:37:56,480 --> 00:37:57,980
you're going to take total control of that person.

588
00:37:58,840 --> 00:38:00,080
With hundreds of applications,

589
00:38:00,960 --> 00:38:03,360
the couboutin can be used in almost any scenario.

590
00:38:04,060 --> 00:38:06,080
Somebody comes up from behind you and grabs you.

591
00:38:06,500 --> 00:38:08,840
She'll press the couboutin down into the elbow area

592
00:38:08,841 --> 00:38:10,560
and then takes control of the wrist.

593
00:38:11,120 --> 00:38:12,560
It's one of many pressure points.

594
00:38:13,080 --> 00:38:15,340
When she presses down, my hand lets go.

595
00:38:16,260 --> 00:38:18,540
No matter how big the guy is, if he grabs you,

596
00:38:18,900 --> 00:38:21,080
you put one of these between his knuckles and pull his hand,

597
00:38:21,100 --> 00:38:22,660
he's going to let go, and he's going to go with that hand.

598
00:38:22,661 --> 00:38:28,380
At first glance, the Wildcat keychain seems harmless, even cute.

599
00:38:29,000 --> 00:38:34,920
But squeeze it inside your fist, and it becomes a devastating self-defense weapon.

600
00:38:36,900 --> 00:38:39,720
Another close-quarters weapon that we sell are stun guns.

601
00:38:40,440 --> 00:38:43,400
Stun guns deliver a disabling electric shock.

602
00:38:44,860 --> 00:38:50,740
Law enforcement has used them for decades, and more recently, the general public.

603
00:38:52,660 --> 00:38:56,220
A stun gun works off a simple 3 or 9 volt battery system.

604
00:38:57,540 --> 00:39:01,340
Energy is sent through a set of capacitors to produce a high voltage current,

605
00:39:01,700 --> 00:39:04,780
from 100,000 volts to more than a million.

606
00:39:05,760 --> 00:39:10,320
The strong electric shock disrupts the signals that go from the brain to the voluntary muscles,

607
00:39:10,940 --> 00:39:12,100
causing them to shut down.

608
00:39:13,280 --> 00:39:15,540
The effects last up to several minutes.

609
00:39:17,660 --> 00:39:21,180
Consumer stun guns come in a variety of tiny shapes and sizes.

610
00:39:21,181 --> 00:39:24,180
This gun here doubles as a cell phone.

611
00:39:24,181 --> 00:39:25,180
Everybody's carrying a cell phone,

612
00:39:25,181 --> 00:39:28,180
but this cell phone has an LED light, which comes in handy,

613
00:39:28,181 --> 00:39:31,180
but even more importantly, it's a stun gun.

614
00:39:31,181 --> 00:39:33,180
What's great about these mini stun guns

615
00:39:33,181 --> 00:39:36,180
is they're small, compact, very concealable,

616
00:39:36,181 --> 00:39:39,180
and they pack a hell of a punch.

617
00:39:39,181 --> 00:39:42,180
Stun guns are considered close-quarter weapons.

618
00:39:42,181 --> 00:39:45,180
When you need a tiny weapon with a longer range,

619
00:39:45,181 --> 00:39:48,180
you can grab a can of pepper spray.

620
00:39:48,181 --> 00:39:57,520
What pepper spray is, is a mixture of very hot peppers with a few other components that cause the body to do things involuntarily.

621
00:39:57,521 --> 00:40:01,512
The eyes will slam shut. Your lungs feel like they're closing up.

622
00:40:01,513 --> 00:40:04,522
Your airways and mucous membranes start to swell.

623
00:40:04,523 --> 00:40:07,040
It takes the fight right out of somebody.

624
00:40:07,940 --> 00:40:12,956
The hot pepper in Irv's pepper spray is rated at 2 million Scoville heat units.

625
00:40:12,957 --> 00:40:15,940
That's 400 times hotter than a jalapeno pepper.

626
00:40:16,800 --> 00:40:19,500
But Irv sells an even more powerful pepper spray.

627
00:40:20,240 --> 00:40:23,520
We call it Black Label Special Tactical Ops.

628
00:40:23,980 --> 00:40:26,460
And what this is for is worst-case scenarios.

629
00:40:26,820 --> 00:40:29,000
We already have a really nasty pepper spray to begin with.

630
00:40:29,400 --> 00:40:31,000
Then you add 2% tear gas.

631
00:40:31,540 --> 00:40:35,360
That combined with pepper is totally for a respiratory takedown.

632
00:40:35,940 --> 00:40:37,860
Tactical teams can hit them with the Black Label

633
00:40:37,861 --> 00:40:41,180
and pretty much incapacitate someone within a half a second or so.

634
00:40:42,420 --> 00:40:44,200
Working with police and civilians,

635
00:40:44,960 --> 00:40:49,460
Irv believes that using less lethal force is the first step in any physical confrontation.

636
00:40:50,200 --> 00:40:51,600
Nobody wants to take a life.

637
00:40:51,960 --> 00:40:56,620
In most situations, if you pull the pepper spray to use it first and it gets ugly fast,

638
00:40:56,740 --> 00:40:58,580
you literally throw the spray and you pull your sidearm.

639
00:40:58,840 --> 00:40:59,540
That's how it's done.

640
00:41:01,640 --> 00:41:04,920
From the city streets to the fields of war,

641
00:41:05,720 --> 00:41:07,400
as weapons get more powerful,

642
00:41:09,720 --> 00:41:11,240
ingenuity shrinks them down.

643
00:41:11,900 --> 00:41:13,820
Making weapons big is easy.

644
00:41:14,200 --> 00:41:20,600
The hard part is trying to make something that works so that one soldier can carry it into battle.

645
00:41:21,080 --> 00:41:28,980
Whether it's for self-defense against a single foe, or full-scale war versus an army of enemies,

646
00:41:30,960 --> 00:41:34,260
tiny weapons have a big place in today's arsenals.

